cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use aiprov, please cite both the software and the F(AI)²R paper."
title: "aiprov: domain-agnostic AI provenance over PROV-O"
type: software
abstract: >-
  aiprov records who, a person or an AI model, did what to an artefact and who checked it, in a plain Turtle file
  as a profile of W3C PROV-O: the vocabulary, the provlog command line (activities with the telemetry the tool
  reports, claims on a seven-step verification ladder whose top two steps only registered humans may grant,
  validate, report, merge) and a dashboard builder.
keywords:
  - provenance
  - PROV-O
  - AI
  - FAIR
  - RDF
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/noheton/aiprov
url: https://w3id.org/aiprov
authors:
  - family-names: Krebs
    given-names: Florian
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6033-801X
    affiliation: "DLR Institute of Structures and Design, ZLP Augsburg"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "F(AI)2R: Who Did What, and Who Checked? Verifiable AI Provenance as an Executable Skill"
    authors:
      - family-names: Krebs
        given-names: Florian
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.48550/arXiv.2607.25637
